WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:01.767
-Ah, you're a stud.

00:00:01.767 --> 00:00:02.934
-What's going on?
-Welcome.

00:00:02.934 --> 00:00:04.567
You're making your late-night
talk show debut.

00:00:04.567 --> 00:00:06.467
-Yes. What's up, y'all?
-This is your debut tonight.

00:00:06.467 --> 00:00:08.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.968 --> 00:00:10.567
-Thank you for choosing
our show.

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:11.968
We appreciate that.

00:00:11.968 --> 00:00:13.801
I know you were here actually
performing.

00:00:13.801 --> 00:00:15.801
You've performed on the show.
-Yes. On that stage.

00:00:15.801 --> 00:00:16.901
-Yeah.
-Over there. Yes.

00:00:16.901 --> 00:00:18.434
-You were in the cast of
"Ain't Too Proud."

00:00:18.434 --> 00:00:20.133
-"Ain't Too Proud." My boys.

00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:22.200
-This is 2019 right there.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:26.167
And this was -- I remember
this show, the Temptations.

00:00:26.167 --> 00:00:28.234
-Yes.
-This was opening night?

00:00:28.234 --> 00:00:29.868
-God, it was opening night.

00:00:29.868 --> 00:00:33.601
Our producers thought it was
a great idea for us to be here,

00:00:33.601 --> 00:00:36.400
get in an old Cadillac and drive
to our opening night

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.934
on 46th Street.

00:00:37.934 --> 00:00:40.734
What they didn't realize was
in this old Cadillac was

00:00:40.734 --> 00:00:44.334
a lot of dust, so as we're
riding from here to 46th,

00:00:44.334 --> 00:00:46.968
all the boys, we start to have
allergy attacks and our throats

00:00:46.968 --> 00:00:48.534
start closing up.
-Oh, my God.

00:00:48.534 --> 00:00:51.501
-We start to panic.
-You're kidding me.

00:00:51.501 --> 00:00:53.968
-One that I'll never forget.
-Yeah.

00:00:53.968 --> 00:00:55.267
Gosh, why would you do that
on opening night?

00:00:55.267 --> 00:00:56.434
-Why would you do that to us?
-I'm so sorry.

00:00:56.434 --> 00:00:57.767
-It's okay.
-But thank you for doing that.

00:00:57.767 --> 00:01:00.267
You went on to be nominated for
a Tony, so there you go.

00:01:00.267 --> 00:01:02.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:02.167 --> 00:01:05.434
Not too shabby.

00:01:05.434 --> 00:01:06.934
Actually, you also got nominated

00:01:06.934 --> 00:01:09.634
for another Tony that night,
right?

00:01:09.634 --> 00:01:11.133
Was it "Ain't Too Proud" --
-At the same time, yeah.

00:01:11.133 --> 00:01:12.667
-At the same time.
And "Choir Boy."

00:01:12.667 --> 00:01:13.534
-Yeah.

00:01:13.534 --> 00:01:14.868
-What was the Tonys like
for you?

00:01:14.868 --> 00:01:16.801
Were you just like "This is it"?
-The Tonys was a blur.

00:01:16.801 --> 00:01:19.200
I mean, my parents were there.
They were so very proud of me.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.701
But it was like a marathon.
I was like running from one side

00:01:21.701 --> 00:01:23.367
of the stage to the other side
of the stage at Radio City.

00:01:23.367 --> 00:01:25.300
I kinda blacked out, hoping that
I didn't win because I had

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:28.167
nothing to say.
I wouldn't know who to thank.

00:01:28.167 --> 00:01:30.467
-Yeah. But you have
very supportive parents?

00:01:30.467 --> 00:01:33.434
-Very supportive.
-Do they come to your premieres?

00:01:33.434 --> 00:01:38.000
-They do, they do.
My mom, who I love so dearly,

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:40.534
my Broadway debut, "Choir Boy,"

00:01:40.534 --> 00:01:42.467
she passed out during the middle
of the show.

00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:43.667
[ Audience aws ]
She's fine.

00:01:43.667 --> 00:01:45.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.133 --> 00:01:47.367
-Did you see her pass out?
-No, it was one of those things

00:01:47.367 --> 00:01:49.334
where, you know, we're doing
our, you know, our thing,

00:01:49.334 --> 00:01:52.367
and we hear kind of on the God
mike from our stage manager,

00:01:52.367 --> 00:01:55.033
"All actors exit the stage."
We do so.

00:01:55.033 --> 00:01:58.133
They tell us, you know, someone
has passed out, they're okay.

00:01:58.133 --> 00:01:59.667
So all the boys were kind of
like,

00:01:59.667 --> 00:02:03.567
"Well, was it an old patron?
Like, how old are they?

00:02:03.567 --> 00:02:05.200
Are they fine?"
-Of course, yeah.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:07.434
-You know what I mean?
We go back, we finish the show.

00:02:07.434 --> 00:02:09.100
It was all of our Broadway
debuts, so it was

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:11.834
my brilliant idea for us to walk
out with "Hi, Mom" signs

00:02:11.834 --> 00:02:13.467
because all of our moms
are there.

00:02:13.467 --> 00:02:16.467
I'm looking out for mine.
I'm assuming she's there.

00:02:16.467 --> 00:02:19.934
I get off the stage, and I see
my brother and stepdad there,

00:02:19.934 --> 00:02:22.334
and they're like, "It was Mom
who passed out."

00:02:22.334 --> 00:02:23.767
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.767 --> 00:02:26.667
And really, she just got so
excited and nervous, I guess,

00:02:26.667 --> 00:02:30.000
moms when they watch their kids
on stage, she didn't want me

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.200
to be nervous, so she wanted to
take all of the nerves.

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:34.133
[ Laughter ]
-And she's proud of you.

00:02:34.133 --> 00:02:36.033
-She's very proud of me.
Apparently as soon as she got up

00:02:36.033 --> 00:02:38.701
from, you know, seeing Jesus
Christ, she came back and --

00:02:38.701 --> 00:02:40.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:41.934
Apparently she said,
"Tell them I'm not going."

00:02:41.934 --> 00:02:44.901
So my mom was in an ambulance
outside of the theater,

00:02:44.901 --> 00:02:46.200
and I was able to give her a hug
and love,

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:47.734
and she made it to the
after-party, so all is good.

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:49.033
-Wow.
-Yeah.

00:02:49.033 --> 00:02:52.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:52.133 --> 00:02:53.200
-That's interesting.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:54.667
You were in "Ain't Too Proud,"

00:02:54.667 --> 00:02:56.100
and then your mom was actually
too proud.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:57.667
-She was so proud.
-Yeah, she was.

00:02:57.667 --> 00:02:59.133
-She got too proud.
-She got too proud.

00:02:59.133 --> 00:03:00.534
Exactly. Yeah.

00:03:00.534 --> 00:03:02.667
I want to talk about,
you're going back to Broadway.

00:03:02.667 --> 00:03:04.267
-Yes.
-Here you are right here

00:03:04.267 --> 00:03:06.334
with "The Collaboration."

00:03:06.334 --> 00:03:08.367
You play Basquiat.

00:03:08.367 --> 00:03:10.767
-Basquiat.
-Basquiat.

00:03:10.767 --> 00:03:12.367
Is that Paul Bettany
as Andy Warhol?

00:03:12.367 --> 00:03:14.567
-It is.
-And you did this in London?

00:03:14.567 --> 00:03:17.734
-Yes. It's been a journey with
this project.

00:03:17.734 --> 00:03:19.734
We went to London
at the Young Vic Theatre.

00:03:19.734 --> 00:03:23.334
We just wrapped the movie
last weekend, and we are in

00:03:23.334 --> 00:03:25.634
rehearsals for the Broadway
production right now.

00:03:25.634 --> 00:03:27.234
-That's wild.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:27.234 --> 00:03:29.033
-He's such an interesting guy
from what I've read.

00:03:29.033 --> 00:03:32.567
-Yeah, he's such a beautiful,
mysterious spirit.

00:03:32.567 --> 00:03:35.167
And the story just follows
the two of them, Andy Warhol

00:03:35.167 --> 00:03:36.701
and Basquiat
and the collaboration they did

00:03:36.701 --> 00:03:38.267
in the '80s in New York.
-Yeah.

00:03:38.267 --> 00:03:39.801
-So, you know, we're just having
a really good time.

00:03:39.801 --> 00:03:41.868
I love Paul so much,
and it's just been, you know,

00:03:41.868 --> 00:03:43.400
a once-in-a-lifetime experience
to do it

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.033
in three different iterations.

00:03:45.033 --> 00:03:46.834
And it keeps evolving,
it keeps evolving.

00:03:46.834 --> 00:03:49.467
So I'm just excited to bring it
to New York.

00:03:49.467 --> 00:03:51.634
-Performances start
November 29th

00:03:51.634 --> 00:03:53.701
at the Samuel J. Friedman
Theatre.

00:03:53.701 --> 00:03:55.734
Congratulations on doing this.

00:03:55.734 --> 00:03:57.701
Let's talk about
"The Inspection."

00:03:57.701 --> 00:03:59.167
-"The Inspection."

00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:01.234
-You're getting great reviews
for this one.

00:04:01.234 --> 00:04:02.434
If you want to plug your ears,

00:04:02.434 --> 00:04:04.067
I'm just gonna talk about you
for a second.

00:04:04.067 --> 00:04:06.501
"Pope gives a career-igniting
performance in the role."

00:04:06.501 --> 00:04:08.334
That was Variety.

00:04:08.334 --> 00:04:11.200
"Pope seems primed for movie
stardom with this turn."

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:13.000
The Wrap. What?

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:16.133
[ Cheers and applause ]
Not too shabby, bud.

00:04:16.133 --> 00:04:19.033
Tony Awards. Come on.
All the awards.

00:04:19.033 --> 00:04:20.534
-It's a blessing.
It's a blessing.

00:04:20.534 --> 00:04:22.300
-Good for you.
This is based on a true story.

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:23.467
Can you set up what this is?

00:04:23.467 --> 00:04:25.901
-Yes, it's based off
of the experiences of

00:04:25.901 --> 00:04:28.367
the writer/director
Elegance Bratton.

00:04:28.367 --> 00:04:31.434
He was kicked out of his house
by his mother for being gay

00:04:31.434 --> 00:04:34.267
and lived homeless for about
15 years and didn't have

00:04:34.267 --> 00:04:36.968
too many options, but the option
he decided to go with was join

00:04:36.968 --> 00:04:41.567
the Marines in an attempt to win
his mother's love and affection.

00:04:41.567 --> 00:04:43.434
He finds self-love,
self-worthiness.

00:04:43.434 --> 00:04:45.267
It's a story that challenges
masculinity

00:04:45.267 --> 00:04:47.067
and what it means to be
yourself.

00:04:47.067 --> 00:04:48.868
We shot it
in Jackson, Mississippi,

00:04:48.868 --> 00:04:51.334
last year in 19 days.

00:04:51.334 --> 00:04:53.300
It was very hot.
-Yeah.

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:55.000
-But I'm so proud of this film.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:56.434
It was made with
such a labor of love.

00:04:56.434 --> 00:04:58.434
A24, Gamechanger Films.

00:04:58.434 --> 00:04:59.634
My cast was incredible.

00:04:59.634 --> 00:05:02.834
Gabrielle Union, Bokeem
Woodbine, Raul Castillo.

00:05:02.834 --> 00:05:04.901
I love them so much.
So we're kind of -- we've been

00:05:04.901 --> 00:05:07.501
able to take it to festivals,
New York Film Festival, TIFF.

00:05:07.501 --> 00:05:11.601
-When you do a movie like this
and it's realistic,

00:05:11.601 --> 00:05:13.434
do you have to train for this?

00:05:13.434 --> 00:05:15.934
-Yeah, well, this one
specifically, boot camp.

00:05:15.934 --> 00:05:18.467
I've never served
in the military,

00:05:18.467 --> 00:05:20.868
so we had some pretty intense
boot camp.

00:05:20.868 --> 00:05:23.234
I remember there was one
morning, you know, we had done

00:05:23.234 --> 00:05:25.701
our readthrough and we got,
you know, our call sheet

00:05:25.701 --> 00:05:27.234
and it said 3:30 a.m. pickup.

00:05:27.234 --> 00:05:29.200
And I was like, "P.M. or A.M.?"

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:30.534
[ Laughter ]
And it was A.M.

00:05:30.534 --> 00:05:34.901
And it was because we were going
out to basically do

00:05:34.901 --> 00:05:37.601
all of the push-ups
and all of the running.

00:05:37.601 --> 00:05:38.701
-So you get a real feel
of the character.

00:05:38.701 --> 00:05:40.033
-To get a real feel of
what it's like.

00:05:40.033 --> 00:05:41.701
And I just wanted to remind
everyone, I'm an actor.

00:05:41.701 --> 00:05:43.667
[ Laughter ]

00:05:43.667 --> 00:05:45.300
I want to learn how to act it.
-"I'm acting.

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:47.367
I'm not actually
in the military.

00:05:47.367 --> 00:05:50.734
I'm acting like I'm in."
You did a very convincing job.

00:05:50.734 --> 00:05:51.834
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:51.834 --> 00:05:53.667
Here's Jeremy Pope
in "The Inspection."

00:05:53.667 --> 00:05:55.234
Take a look at this.

00:05:55.234 --> 00:05:56.501
-My mom.

00:05:59.334 --> 00:06:01.501
She won't even talk to me.

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:11.234
Most of my friends
are dead or in jail.

00:06:12.534 --> 00:06:14.467
The streets is going to kill me
no matter what,

00:06:14.467 --> 00:06:17.901
so if I die in this uniform...

00:06:20.267 --> 00:06:23.000
...I'm a hero to somebody.

00:06:24.901 --> 00:06:27.534
-Oof.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:27.534 --> 00:06:29.467
Jeremy Pope!

00:06:29.467 --> 00:06:31.734
"The Inspection" opens
in select theaters

00:06:31.734 --> 00:06:34.434
this Friday,
nationwide December 2nd.

00:06:34.434 --> 00:06:37.567
Thank you so much, bud.
Come back, please, okay?

00:06:37.567 --> 00:06:39.801
Bruce Springsteen performs
for us after the break!

00:06:39.801 --> 00:06:41.133
Stick around, everybody.

